Usage: hudiff <command> [flags]

diffs for humans — an agent explains a diff, you comment on it line by line in
the browser, the comments flow back.

Commands:
  workspace          Working tree vs HEAD, staged included (the default,
                     no verb).
  commit             A single commit against its first parent.
  range              A range: <a>..<b>, <a>...<b>, or just <a> vs the working
                     tree.
  pr                 A GitHub pull request.
  patch              A patch file or stdin.
  files              Two files or two directories on disk; no repository needed.
  open               Reopen an existing session in the viewer.
  session list       List sessions.
  session info       Print session info.
  session url        Print the session URL, starting the daemon if needed.
  session refresh    Re-read the diff and re-anchor comments.
  session archive    Archive a session; the data and link stay.
  session rm         Delete sessions, comments included.
  read               Print the diff with [file#hunk] tags and both line-number
                     columns.
  context            Repo-level context: recent history, changed symbols,
                     callers, tests.
  notes              Write the agent's per-hunk explanation.
  diagram            List, dump or render diagrams.
  review show        Show the report.
  review set         Write a report; merges into the existing one by default.
  review done        Mark an item handled.
  review wontfix     Mark an item wontfix.
  review reopen      Reopen an item.
  review note        Append a re-review note to an item.
  review md          Export the report as markdown.
  comments           List comments.
  wait               Block until the user hits Send, then print the new
                     comments.
  reply              Reply to a comment.
  resolve            Mark a comment handled, awaiting the user's confirmation.
  agents list        List the agents running in this repo.
  agents deliver     Type a command into the terminal an agent is running in.
  daemon start       Start the daemon if it is not running.
  daemon stop        Stop the daemon; session data is kept.
  daemon restart     Stop it and start it again on the same port.
  daemon status      Print URL, port and pid.
  skill path         Print the skill path, materialising it if needed.
  skill install      Install the skill for an agent.
  config path        Print the config file path.
  config show        Print the effective config.
  config init        Write a config file with the defaults.
  version            Print the version.

Flags:
  -h, --help            Show context-sensitive help.
  -s, --session=<id>    Session id; default = most recent in this repo.
      --port=<n>        Daemon port; only used when the daemon has to be
                        started.

Run "hudiff <command> --help" for more information on a command.
